🧠 CognitiveAIOps: Executive FAQ

Q1: How does CognitiveAIOps handle RBAC and ABAC across different enterprise apps?
A: We don’t impose a one-size-fits-all RBAC layer.
CognitiveAIOps learns entitlements directly from user behavior and system responses.
Each action—like “approve audit” or “escalate risk”—is logged with who triggered it, which UI event occurred, and what API or state was allowed.
From this, a learned RBAC/ABAC manifest is automatically generated and refined over time, defining context-aware gates (e.g., “Approve only if status=Submitted and role=Manager”).
This creates a self-evolving, auditable entitlement layer unique to each application.

Q2: How is CognitiveAIOps different from chatbots or workflow automation?
A: It’s not a chatbot—it’s an agentic AI ecosystem.
CognitiveAIOps learns from real user actions, reasons across multiple systems, adapts to business context, and orchestrates tasks spanning Risk, Audit, Fraud, and Issue Management.
It’s like giving every enterprise app an AI brain that understands your processes end-to-end.

Q3: What does “federated AI” mean in this context?
A: Each enterprise system hosts its own specialized agentic model.
The federated layer (powered by LangGraph) lets these agents collaborate securely, share insights, and reason together—without moving data out of its domain.
This ensures local compliance with global intelligence.

Q4: How do external tools like JIRA, ServiceNow, or PTS integrate?
A: CognitiveAIOps uses a manifest-based integration model.
Admins define external domains, APIs, and policies directly in configuration—no code changes.
This allows seamless cross-platform actions (e.g., risk escalation auto-creates a JIRA ticket or syncs a fraud case to PTS) under unified audit and RBAC controls.

Q5: How are new workflows onboarded or updated?
A: Entirely declaratively.
SMEs update YAML manifests (AAM_Workflows.yaml) to define steps, actions, and conditions—no redeployments or coding required.
Changes in policy or regulation can be propagated instantly across all relevant agents.

Q6: How does the platform ensure governance and compliance?
A: Each manifest (RBAC, ABAC, logging, and policy) defines what’s allowed, when, and by whom.
The Governance Engine enforces these rules in real time, creating immutable audit trails and complete traceability—ideal for regulatory environments.

Q7: How does CognitiveAIOps improve productivity and business outcomes?
A: Every user and system action generates telemetry.
Dashboards track time-to-resolution, automation vs. manual effort, bottlenecks, and efficiency trends—helping management identify automation opportunities and measure ROI.

Q8: How do humans stay in control of automation?
A: Human-in-the-loop is core.
Flows can require manual confirmation or dual approvals, and SMEs can pause or override any agentic action.
AI suggests; humans decide.

Q9: What happens if one model or domain fails?
A: Fault tolerance is built-in.
Each domain agent works independently, while the federated layer reroutes requests or switches to manual mode—ensuring continuous operations.

Q10: What’s the ROI compared to traditional AI platforms?
A: No rip-and-replace.
CognitiveAIOps builds on your existing systems, reducing time-to-automation from months to days.
Organizations typically see 30–40% faster case resolution and 25% improved governance adherence within months of rollout.
